00:51:00.457 --> 00:51:02.759
TO INCLUDE A DETAILED RISK
ANALYSIS

00:51:02.826 --> 00:51:04.060
ASSESSMENT PROCEDURE.

00:51:04.127 --> 00:51:07.164
EXCUSE ME FOR PROCURING
AUTOMATED DECISION

00:51:07.230 --> 00:51:10.133
SYSTEMS OR ADDS ANALYZE SPECIFIC

00:51:10.200 --> 00:51:12.402
CHARACTERISTICS OF THE ADDS
METHODS

00:51:12.469 --> 00:51:14.070
FOR APPROPRIATE RISK CONTROLS,

00:51:14.137 --> 00:51:17.574
AND EXAMINE ADVERSE INCIDENT
MONITORING PROCEDURES.

00:51:17.641 --> 00:51:19.876
SPECIFICALLY, THE BILL REQUIRES

00:51:20.677 --> 00:51:22.379
THAT IT IT DOES THREE THINGS.

00:51:22.446 --> 00:51:24.314
FIRST, IT WOULD ASSESS THE RISKS
ASSOCIATED

00:51:24.381 --> 00:51:26.683
WITH PROCURING HIGH RISK, I
ADDS,

00:51:26.750 --> 00:51:28.251
PARTICULARLY IN AREAS THAT HAVE
A HIGH

00:51:28.318 --> 00:51:29.953
IMPACT ON INDIVIDUALS RIGHTS,

00:51:30.020 --> 00:51:32.189
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO
HEALTH, EDUCATION,

00:51:32.255 --> 00:51:34.357
EMPLOYMENT, INSURANCE,
UTILITIES,

00:51:34.424 --> 00:51:36.927
CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE, PUBLIC
SERVICES,

00:51:36.993 --> 00:51:38.662
AND JUSTICE OR LEGAL SERVICES.

00:51:38.728 --> 00:51:41.364
SECOND, IT REQUIRES THE
DEVELOPMENT AND ADOPTION OF

00:51:41.431 --> 00:51:44.501
A RISK MANAGEMENT STANDARD THAT
INCLUDES ASSESSMENT,

00:51:44.568 --> 00:51:47.370
APPROPRIATE RISK CONTROLS AND
ADVERSE INCIDENT

00:51:47.437 --> 00:51:49.940
MONITORING WHEN PROCURING SUCH
SYSTEMS.

00:51:50.006 --> 00:51:51.374
AND THIRD, IT WOULD REQUIRE

00:51:51.441 --> 00:51:53.043
THE ENGAGEMENT AND CONSULTATION

00:51:53.109 --> 00:51:54.611
WITH THE DIVERSITY OF
STAKEHOLDERS,

00:51:54.678 --> 00:51:56.880
INCLUDING THOSE MOST AFFECTED BY

00:51:56.947 --> 00:51:58.482
GOVERNMENT USE OF THESE SYSTEMS,

00:51:58.548 --> 00:52:00.684
SUCH AS PUBLIC TRUST AND SAFETY
EXPERTS,

00:52:00.750 --> 00:52:02.252
COMMUNITY BASED ORGANIZATIONS,

00:52:02.319 --> 00:52:03.753
CIVIL SOCIETY GROUPS,

00:52:03.820 --> 00:52:06.223
WORKERS AND ACADEMIC
RESEARCHERS.

00:52:07.424 --> 00:52:08.992
AI TECHNOLOGY THAT IS PROCURED

00:52:09.059 --> 00:52:10.494
AND DEPLOYED RESPONSIBLY

00:52:10.560 --> 00:52:12.362
HAS THE OPPORTUNITY TO
REVOLUTIONIZE

00:52:12.429 --> 00:52:14.531
NOT JUST HOW WE ADMINISTER
GOVERNMENT SERVICES,

00:52:14.598 --> 00:52:15.966
BUT OUR ENTIRE ECONOMY.

00:52:16.032 --> 00:52:18.468
THIS TECHNOLOGY CAN ALSO POSE,
HOWEVER,

00:52:18.535 --> 00:52:20.003
SIGNIFICANT RISKS TO SAFETY,

00:52:20.070 --> 00:52:22.839
PRIVACY AND CIVIL RIGHTS OF
CALIFORNIANS,

00:52:22.906 --> 00:52:24.574
ESPECIALLY WHEN IT'S USED TO
ASSIST

00:52:24.641 --> 00:52:26.610
OR REPLACE HUMAN DECISION MAKING

00:52:26.676 --> 00:52:28.311
IN CRITICAL SECTORS SUCH AS
HOUSING,

00:52:28.378 --> 00:52:30.146
EMPLOYMENT AND HEALTH CARE.

00:52:30.213 --> 00:52:31.748
AS THESE APPLICATIONS OF THESE

00:52:31.815 --> 00:52:32.849
SYSTEMS WILL BE VARIED,

00:52:32.916 --> 00:52:34.417
THE RISK ASSESSMENT AND
SUBSEQUENT

00:52:34.484 --> 00:52:36.353
RISK CONTROLS MUST BE TAILORED

00:52:36.419 --> 00:52:39.356
AND MUST BE UNIQUE TO THE
TECHNOLOGY IN QUESTION.

00:52:39.422 --> 00:52:41.091
THIS STEP IS CRITICAL STEP AS

00:52:41.157 --> 00:52:42.859
WE DETERMINE WHAT AI PRODUCTS

00:52:42.926 --> 00:52:45.929
ARE SAFE FOR GOVERNMENT
PROCUREMENT AND DEPLOYMENT.

00:52:46.463 --> 00:52:47.964
NOT ONLY WILL THIS STRICT
SCRUTINY

00:52:48.031 --> 00:52:49.566
PROTECT THE STATE FROM
LIABILITY,

00:52:49.633 --> 00:52:51.635
BUT IT WILL ALSO HELP ASSURE
THE PUBLIC

00:52:51.701 --> 00:52:53.503
THAT THE TECHNOLOGY THAT WE ARE

00:52:53.570 --> 00:52:55.572
ACQUIRING ON THEIR BEHALF HAS
BEEN

00:52:55.639 --> 00:52:57.541
ASSESSED WITH SAFETY IN MIND.

00:52:57.607 --> 00:52:59.242
INDEED, WE NEED TO IMPLEMENT

00:52:59.309 --> 00:53:00.477
THESE RISK ASSESSMENT TESTS

00:53:00.544 --> 00:53:03.480
AS SOON AS POSSIBLE AND ISSUES
WITH THIS TECHNOLOGY,

00:53:03.547 --> 00:53:05.549
WHICH HAVE ALREADY OCCURRED
IN 2022,

00:53:05.615 --> 00:53:08.552
THE LAO FOUND THAT CALIFORNIA
ED,

00:53:08.618 --> 00:53:10.287
THE EMPLOYMENT DEVELOPMENT
DEPARTMENT,

00:53:10.353 --> 00:53:11.821
PROCURED AN AUTOMATED REVIEW

00:53:11.888 --> 00:53:13.823
SOFTWARE THAT FLAGGED 1.1

00:53:13.890 --> 00:53:16.126
MILLION CLAIMS AS FRAUDULENT,

00:53:16.192 --> 00:53:18.762
MEANING WORKERS STOPPED
RECEIVING THEIR BENEFITS

00:53:18.828 --> 00:53:21.665
AT A CRITICAL TIME TO THEM AND
THEIR FAMILIES.

00:53:21.731 --> 00:53:23.900
ULTIMATELY, MORE THAN HALF OF
THOSE CLAIMS,

00:53:23.967 --> 00:53:27.203
OVER 600,000, WERE CONFIRMED AS
LEGITIMATE.

00:53:27.437 --> 00:53:29.339
THE HARDSHIP THAT THESE
ERRONEOUS

00:53:29.406 --> 00:53:30.407
FINDINGS CREATED COULD

00:53:30.473 --> 00:53:32.409
HAVE BEEN FORESEEN AND AVOIDED
THROUGH PROPER RISK

00:53:32.475 --> 00:53:35.512
ASSESSMENT BEFORE IT WAS GRANTED
ACCESS TO CONTROL,

00:53:35.579 --> 00:53:38.582
A LIFELINE THAT MILLIONS OF
FAMILIES DEPENDED UPON.

00:53:38.648 --> 00:53:42.352
BY ENACTING THESE SAFEGUARDS
PROPOSED BY SB 892,

00:53:42.419 --> 00:53:45.055
CALIFORNIA CAN SET A NATIONAL
STANDARD

00:53:45.121 --> 00:53:46.289
THAT DRIVES INNOVATION OF

00:53:46.356 --> 00:53:48.491
AI TECHNOLOGY AND SERVICES WHILE

00:53:48.558 --> 00:53:49.459
PROTECTING THE PUBLIC

00:53:49.526 --> 00:53:51.595
FROM RISKS POSED BY AUTOMATED

00:53:51.661 --> 00:53:53.263
DECISION MAKING SYSTEMS.

00:53:53.330 --> 00:53:55.332
WITH ME TODAY IS SAMANTHA GORDON
FROM

00:53:55.398 --> 00:53:56.933
THE TECH EQUITY COLLABORATIVE.

00:53:59.970 --> 00:54:00.870
GOOD MORNING.

00:54:00.937 --> 00:54:02.138
GOOD MORNING, CHAIRMAN DODD

00:54:02.205 --> 00:54:03.139
AND MEMBERS OF THE COMMITTEE,

00:54:03.206 --> 00:54:04.874
THANK YOU FOR THE OPPORTUNITY
TO SPEAK TO YOU

00:54:04.941 --> 00:54:08.345
ABOUT SB 892 AND THE IMPORTANCE
OF SETTING STANDARDS

00:54:08.411 --> 00:54:11.548
FOR PUBLIC SECTOR PROCUREMENT
OF AI SYSTEMS.

00:54:11.748 --> 00:54:13.483
AS THE SENATOR SAID, I'M
SAMANTHA GORDON,

00:54:13.550 --> 00:54:14.784
I'M THE CHIEF PROGRAM OFFICER

00:54:14.851 --> 00:54:16.353
AT TECH EQUITY COLLABORATIVE.

00:54:16.419 --> 00:54:18.455
OUR MISSION IS TO RAISE PUBLIC
CONSCIOUSNESS

00:54:18.521 --> 00:54:19.789
ABOUT ECONOMIC EQUITY

00:54:19.856 --> 00:54:21.358
ISSUES IN THE TECH INDUSTRY'S

00:54:21.424 --> 00:54:22.859
PRODUCTS AND PRACTICES,

00:54:22.926 --> 00:54:25.829
AND ENSURE TECHNOLOGY'S GROWTH
BENEFITS EVERYONE.

00:54:25.895 --> 00:54:28.198
WE'RE PROUD TO SUPPORT SB 892 IN

00:54:28.264 --> 00:54:29.566
THIS COMMITTEE TO ENSURE THAT AS

00:54:29.633 --> 00:54:32.369
CALIFORNIA LOOKS TO ADOPT AI
SYSTEMS

00:54:32.435 --> 00:54:33.870
AND EMERGING TECHNOLOGY,

00:54:33.937 --> 00:54:35.271
WE CAN BUILD A CLEAR SET OF

00:54:35.338 --> 00:54:36.506
STANDARDS THAT CAN BENEFIT

00:54:36.573 --> 00:54:39.442
ALL CALIFORNIANS IN ORDER TO
MAKE THE MOST

00:54:39.509 --> 00:54:42.012
OF THE OPPORTUNITY THAT THESE
TECHNOLOGIES PRESENT

00:54:42.078 --> 00:54:44.648
AND SPUR INNOVATION IN OUR
STATE'S SERVICES,

00:54:44.714 --> 00:54:47.384
WE MUST FIRST ENSURE THAT WE
PLACE COMMON SENSE

00:54:47.450 --> 00:54:50.253
GUARDRAILS AROUND THE USE OF
THIS TECHNOLOGY.

00:54:50.320 --> 00:54:52.856
AND THE PUBLIC SECTOR IS RIGHTLY
FOCUSED ON REDUCING

00:54:52.922 --> 00:54:55.925
BACKLOGS AND IMPROVING SERVICES
FOR OUR COMMUNITIES.

00:54:55.992 --> 00:54:57.193
AND I THINK IN THAT REGARD,

00:54:57.260 --> 00:54:59.262
TECHNOLOGY CAN BE REALLY
APPEALING.

00:54:59.329 --> 00:55:00.797
BUT WE ALSO THINK IT'S IMPORTANT

00:55:00.864 --> 00:55:02.399
TO LEARN FROM SEVERAL EXAMPLES

00:55:02.465 --> 00:55:05.135
WHERE THE RAPID ADOPTION OF
TECHNOLOGY

00:55:05.201 --> 00:55:06.269
OFTEN I'LL MENTION,

00:55:06.336 --> 00:55:09.005
WITHOUT SERIOUS INPUT FROM
WORKERS AND COMMUNITIES,

00:55:09.072 --> 00:55:11.574
DRAG THE PUBLIC SECTOR IN THE
OPPOSITE DIRECTION,

00:55:11.641 --> 00:55:12.976
CREATING MASSIVE DELAYS,

00:55:13.043 --> 00:55:15.779
WRONGFUL DENIALS AND VERY COSTLY
PROBLEMS THAT

00:55:15.845 --> 00:55:18.114
THEN THE TAXPAYERS ARE
RESPONSIBLE FOR FIXING.

00:55:18.181 --> 00:55:19.582
SO THE SENATOR JUST MENTIONED

00:55:19.649 --> 00:55:21.017
A KEY EXAMPLE THAT I THINK IS

00:55:21.084 --> 00:55:22.719
WORTH UNDERSCORING AND WAS
BROUGHT

00:55:22.786 --> 00:55:24.254
UP EARLIER ABOUT ED.

00:55:24.320 --> 00:55:27.223
WE SAW MASSIVE ISSUES DURING THE
PANDEMIC OF PEOPLE

00:55:27.290 --> 00:55:29.092
NOT BEING ABLE TO ACCESS THEIR
BENEFITS.

00:55:29.159 --> 00:55:30.593
AND THE DEPARTMENT BROUGHT ON

00:55:30.660 --> 00:55:32.262
A FRAUD DETECTION ALGORITHM
THAT,

00:55:32.328 --> 00:55:35.031
AS THE SENATOR SAID, REVIEWED
10 MILLION CLAIMS.

00:55:35.098 --> 00:55:35.699
RIGHT.

00:55:35.765 --> 00:55:36.733
IT REPLACED THE WORK OF A LOT

00:55:36.800 --> 00:55:38.301
OF HUMANS TO MOVE QUICKLY.

00:55:38.368 --> 00:55:41.671
IT FOUND 1.1 MILLION OF THOSE
WERE FRAUDULENT.

00:55:41.738 --> 00:55:43.640
THEY CUT OFF THE WORKERS
PAYMENTS,

00:55:43.707 --> 00:55:45.442
DIDN'T PROVIDE NOTICE TO THOSE
WORKERS,

00:55:45.508 --> 00:55:48.978
BUT 600,000 OF THOSE WORKERS
CLAIMS WERE LEGITIMATE.

00:55:49.045 --> 00:55:50.980
AND THIS IS NOT UNIQUE TO
CALIFORNIA.

00:55:51.047 --> 00:55:52.916
THAT TECHNOLOGY WAS MARKETED
AND SOLD

00:55:52.982 --> 00:55:54.751
TO 42 STATES IN THIS COUNTRY.

00:55:54.818 --> 00:55:56.486
IT'S CURRENTLY THE SUBJECT OF
A COMPLAINT

00:55:56.553 --> 00:55:58.088
AT THE FEDERAL TRADE COMMISSION.

00:55:58.154 --> 00:55:59.589
AND WE THINK THAT'S IMPORTANT
TO SAY

00:55:59.656 --> 00:56:02.025
BECAUSE AS A STATE OF
CALIFORNIA,

00:56:02.092 --> 00:56:04.694
WE HAVE A MASSIVE, MASSIVE
OPERATION HERE.

00:56:04.761 --> 00:56:06.896
WE'RE THE FIFTH LARGEST ECONOMY
IN THE WORLD, RIGHT?

00:56:06.963 --> 00:56:09.933
SO WE ARE GOING TO BE RECEIVING
A LOT OF MARKETING,

00:56:09.999 --> 00:56:11.534
OF A LOT OF PRODUCTS THAT
PROMISE

00:56:11.601 --> 00:56:12.902
A LOT OF EFFICIENCIES.

00:56:12.969 --> 00:56:14.637
AND WE WANT TO MAKE SURE WE ARE
PUTTING

00:56:14.704 --> 00:56:16.172
REALLY CLEAR STANDARDS IN PLACE

00:56:16.239 --> 00:56:18.875
TO ASSESS FOR THE RISK AND NOT
PUTTING

00:56:18.942 --> 00:56:21.511
THAT BURDEN ON THE TAXPAYERS.

00:56:21.745 --> 00:56:24.681
ANOTHER EXAMPLE IS RECENT FROM
NEW YORK CITY.

00:56:24.748 --> 00:56:27.350
THEY INCORPORATED AN AI POWERED
CHATBOT

00:56:27.417 --> 00:56:28.685
MEANT TO PROVIDE RESIDENTS WITH

00:56:28.752 --> 00:56:30.453
INFORMATION ABOUT STARTING AND
OPERATING

00:56:30.520 --> 00:56:31.755
A BUSINESS IN THE CITY.

00:56:31.821 --> 00:56:33.656
WITHIN FIVE MONTHS, IT WAS FOUND

00:56:33.723 --> 00:56:35.058
THAT THE CHATBOT REPEATEDLY

00:56:35.125 --> 00:56:36.493
PROVIDED ADVICE TO THE PUBLIC

00:56:36.559 --> 00:56:38.328
TO EXPLICITLY BREAK THE LAW.

00:56:38.394 --> 00:56:40.196
SO QUESTIONS LIKE CAN I TAKE

00:56:40.263 --> 00:56:41.831
A CUT OF MY WORKERS TIPS?

00:56:41.898 --> 00:56:44.100
WOULD GET AN ANSWER FROM THE
CHATBOT THAT SAID,

00:56:44.167 --> 00:56:46.302
YES, YOU CAN TAKE A CUT OF YOUR
WORKERS

00:56:46.369 --> 00:56:49.005
TIPS AND PROVIDED CONFUSING BUT
LEGAL SOUNDING

00:56:49.072 --> 00:56:51.708
JUSTIFICATION FOR THIS ILLEGAL
PRACTICE.

00:56:51.775 --> 00:56:53.309
OR QUESTIONS ABOUT HOUSING.

00:56:53.376 --> 00:56:55.044
LIKE DO LANDLORDS HAVE TO ACCEPT

00:56:55.111 --> 00:56:56.679
TENANTS ON RENTAL ASSISTANCE?

00:56:56.746 --> 00:56:59.616
CHATBOT WOULD RESPOND NO,
LANDLORDS DO NOT HAVE

00:56:59.682 --> 00:57:02.218
TO ACCEPT TENANTS ON RENTAL
ASSISTANCE,

00:57:02.285 --> 00:57:03.620
WHICH IS FOR THE MOST PART,

00:57:03.686 --> 00:57:05.855
A DIRECT VIOLATION OF A LAW THAT
SAID LANDLORDS

00:57:05.922 --> 00:57:08.391
CANNOT DISCRIMINATE BASED ON
SOURCE OF INCOME.

00:57:08.958 --> 00:57:10.627
WHAT DISTINGUISHES THE PUBLIC

00:57:10.693 --> 00:57:11.795
SECTOR FROM THE PRIVATE

00:57:11.861 --> 00:57:14.531
ACTORS WHO DEVELOP AND SELL THIS
TECHNOLOGY

00:57:14.597 --> 00:57:16.232
IS THAT THE PUBLIC SECTOR IS
RESPONSIBLE

00:57:16.299 --> 00:57:18.301
FOR PROVIDING SERVICES TO
EVERYONE,

00:57:18.368 --> 00:57:20.637
AND ENSURING THAT THOSE SERVICES
ARE SAFE

00:57:20.703 --> 00:57:22.839
AND NOT GOING TO FURTHER HARM
IN OUR LIVES.

00:57:22.906 --> 00:57:24.274
I THINK ALL OF YOU KNOW WELL,

00:57:24.340 --> 00:57:26.476
YOU HEAR FROM YOUR CONSTITUENTS
REGULARLY.

00:57:26.543 --> 00:57:27.777
OUR COMMUNITIES COUNT ON US IN

00:57:27.844 --> 00:57:29.045
SOME OF THE MOST CHALLENGING

00:57:29.112 --> 00:57:31.314
AND VULNERABLE MOMENTS OF THEIR
LIVES,

00:57:31.381 --> 00:57:33.616
AND THEY CANNOT BE USED AS
MARKET

00:57:33.683 --> 00:57:35.084
RESEARCH OR EXPERIMENTS

00:57:35.151 --> 00:57:36.853
FOR THESE PRIVATE COMPANIES WHO

00:57:36.920 --> 00:57:38.421
ARE SELLING AN ALGORITHM.

00:57:38.688 --> 00:57:41.958
SB 882 RECOGNIZES THIS REALITY
AND CALLS FOR

00:57:42.025 --> 00:57:44.160
CLEAR STANDARDS FOR THE USE OF
AUTOMATED

00:57:44.227 --> 00:57:46.362
DECISION MAKING AND AI SYSTEMS

00:57:46.429 --> 00:57:47.864
IN HIGH RISK ENVIRONMENTS,

00:57:47.931 --> 00:57:49.098
AND WE URGE YOUR SUPPORT.

00:57:49.165 --> 00:57:49.933
THANK YOU.

00:57:49.999 --> 00:57:50.800
THANK YOU.

00:57:51.067 --> 00:57:54.170
ANYBODY ELSE WISHING TO TESTIFY
IN SUPPORT?

00:57:54.470 --> 00:57:55.271
SEEING NONE.

00:57:55.338 --> 00:57:58.675
ANYBODY WISHING TO SPEAK AGAINST
THIS BILL.

00:57:58.908 --> 00:57:59.609
SEEING NONE.

00:57:59.676 --> 00:58:01.578
WE'LL MOVE BACK TO THE
COMMITTEE.

00:58:02.846 --> 00:58:03.613
ANY QUESTIONS?

00:58:03.680 --> 00:58:04.681
COMMENTS?

00:58:05.315 --> 00:58:06.382
SEEING NONE.

00:58:06.449 --> 00:58:07.984
SENATOR PADILLA, WOULD YOU LIKE
TO CLOSE?

00:58:08.051 --> 00:58:08.551
THANK YOU, MR.

00:58:08.618 --> 00:58:09.452
CHAIRMAN.

00:58:09.519 --> 00:58:11.020
I APPRECIATE MY WITNESS AND
RESPECTFULLY

00:58:11.087 --> 00:58:12.055
ASK FOR AN I VOTE.

00:58:12.355 --> 00:58:13.156
ALL RIGHT.

00:58:13.523 --> 00:58:14.958
DO WE HAVE A MOTION?

00:58:16.492 --> 00:58:19.028
THIS IS A MOTION BY JOE BORG.

00:58:19.262 --> 00:58:19.963
SENATOR.

00:58:20.029 --> 00:58:20.964
THANK YOU.

