00:59:13.383 --> 00:59:14.050
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU, MR.

00:59:14.117 --> 00:59:14.517
CHAIR.

00:59:14.584 --> 00:59:15.418
COMMITTEE MEMBERS.

00:59:15.485 --> 00:59:17.320
UH, WE'D LIKE TO START BY NOTING
THAT WE'LL

00:59:17.387 --> 00:59:19.355
BE ACCEPTING THE COMMITTEE
AMENDMENTS.

00:59:19.622 --> 00:59:22.325
SB 1402 WOULD REQUIRE ALL STATE
AGENCIES,

00:59:22.392 --> 00:59:24.093
DEPARTMENTS, BOARDS, OFFICES,

00:59:24.160 --> 00:59:26.596
COMMISSIONS AND CONSERVANCIES
TO CONSIDER

00:59:26.663 --> 00:59:29.032
THE 30 BY 30 GOALS WHEN
ADOPTING,

00:59:29.098 --> 00:59:31.067
REVISING OR ESTABLISHING THEIR
PLANS,

00:59:31.134 --> 00:59:33.369
POLICIES OR REGULATIONS WHICH

00:59:33.436 --> 00:59:34.704
DIRECTLY AFFECT LAND USE,

00:59:34.771 --> 00:59:36.072
NATURAL RESOURCE MANAGEMENT,

00:59:36.139 --> 00:59:37.473
WATER USE, AND QUALITY,

00:59:37.540 --> 00:59:39.709
AND BIODIVERSITY CONSERVATION.

00:59:40.109 --> 00:59:42.111
CALIFORNIA IS HOME TO ONE OF 25

00:59:42.178 --> 00:59:44.047
GLOBAL BIODIVERSITY HOTSPOTS,

00:59:44.113 --> 00:59:45.682
BUT THIS BIODIVERSITY IS UNDER

00:59:45.748 --> 00:59:46.916
THREAT FROM CLIMATE CHANGE,

00:59:46.983 --> 00:59:50.787
HABITAT LOSS AND FRAGMENTATION,
INVASIVE SPECIES,

00:59:50.853 --> 00:59:52.822
DISEASE, PESTS AND POLLUTION.

00:59:52.889 --> 00:59:54.958
CONSERVATION IS ONE OF THE BEST
TOOLS

00:59:55.024 --> 00:59:56.426
THAT WE HAVE TO PREVENT FURTHER

00:59:56.492 --> 00:59:58.895
EXTINCTIONS AND PROTECT OUR
BIODIVERSITY

00:59:58.962 --> 01:00:00.263
AND ECOSYSTEMS.

01:00:00.330 --> 01:00:02.732
IN 2020, GOVERNOR NEWSOM ISSUED
EXECUTIVE

01:00:02.799 --> 01:00:06.703
ORDER NUMBER N 8220 TO ADOPT
A GOAL TO

01:00:06.769 --> 01:00:09.172
CONSERVE AT LEAST 30% OF
CALIFORNIA'S LAND

01:00:09.238 --> 01:00:11.641
AND COASTAL WATERS BY THE YEAR
2030.

01:00:11.708 --> 01:00:14.043
TO ENSURE THIS GOAL REMAINED
A COMMITMENT

01:00:14.110 --> 01:00:15.545
FOR FUTURE ADMINISTRATIONS.

01:00:15.611 --> 01:00:18.614
LAST YEAR, I AUTHORED SB 337
TO CODIFY

01:00:18.681 --> 01:00:21.084
THIS 30 BY 30 GOAL INTO STATUTE.

01:00:21.150 --> 01:00:22.952
WHILE CALIFORNIA HAS MADE
CRITICAL INVESTMENTS

01:00:23.019 --> 01:00:25.421
IN CONSERVATION TO FURTHER THIS
30 BY 30 GOAL,

01:00:25.488 --> 01:00:26.723
IT'S IMPORTANT THAT THIS GOAL

01:00:26.789 --> 01:00:28.157
ALSO BE ROOTED IN THE PLANS,

01:00:28.224 --> 01:00:30.626
POLICIES AND REGULATIONS OF OUR
STATE AGENCIES.

01:00:30.693 --> 01:00:32.528
TODAY, I HAVE WITH ME AARON
WOOLLEY,

01:00:32.595 --> 01:00:34.764
SENIOR POLICY STRATEGIST FOR
SIERRA CLUB,

01:00:34.831 --> 01:00:37.300
TO TESTIFY IN SUPPORT OF SB
1402.

01:00:37.533 --> 01:00:38.568
&GT;&GT; GOOD MORNING.

01:00:38.634 --> 01:00:39.969
GOOD MORNING, CHAIR DODD,
MEMBERS OF THE COMMITTEE.

01:00:40.036 --> 01:00:42.005
MY NAME IS AARON WOOLLEY, AND
I'M A SENIOR POLICY

01:00:42.071 --> 01:00:43.606
STRATEGIST WITH SIERRA CLUB
CALIFORNIA.

01:00:43.673 --> 01:00:44.941
SPEAKING TODAY ON BEHALF OF
OUR HALF

01:00:45.008 --> 01:00:47.877
A MILLION MEMBERS AND
SUPPORTERS, UM,

01:00:47.944 --> 01:00:49.479
I'D LIKE TO THANK SENATOR MANN
FOR

01:00:49.545 --> 01:00:50.813
SPONSORING THIS LEGISLATION

01:00:50.880 --> 01:00:53.216
AND FOR THE CONTINUED SUPPORT
FOR 30 BY 30.

01:00:53.282 --> 01:00:56.452
CALIFORNIA HAS AN AMBITIOUS
VISION OF PROTECTING

01:00:56.519 --> 01:00:58.654
30% OF OUR LANDS AND WATERS BY

01:00:58.721 --> 01:01:01.424
2030 TO COMBAT THE DUAL CLIMATE
AND BIODIVERSITY

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:03.659
CRISIS IMPACTING OUR STATE.

01:01:03.860 --> 01:01:05.895
SB 337, WHICH PASSED LAST YEAR,

01:01:05.962 --> 01:01:09.632
CODIFIED 30 BY 30 AS A GOAL AND
SB 1402,

01:01:09.699 --> 01:01:11.234
BUILDS ON THAT POLICY BY
ENSURING

01:01:11.300 --> 01:01:12.769
THAT GOAL IS ALSO CONSIDERED

01:01:12.835 --> 01:01:14.670
BY KEY AGENCIES AND OTHER STATE
DECISION

01:01:14.737 --> 01:01:16.739
MAKING BODIES DURING PROCESSES

01:01:16.806 --> 01:01:18.741
TO UPDATE OR ESTABLISH PLANS,

01:01:18.808 --> 01:01:20.443
POLICIES AND REGULATIONS.

01:01:20.510 --> 01:01:22.745
ACTING IN SILOS IS NOT AN
EFFECTIVE

01:01:22.812 --> 01:01:24.313
POLICY MAKING STRATEGIES.

01:01:24.380 --> 01:01:26.549
STATE AGENCIES, BOARDS AND
COMMISSIONS ARE ALREADY

01:01:26.616 --> 01:01:28.818
RESPONSIBLE FOR MANAGING OUR
PUBLIC LANDS,

01:01:28.885 --> 01:01:30.920
ENSURING OUR RIVERS, LAKES AND
COASTS ARE

01:01:30.987 --> 01:01:33.756
CLEAN AND PROTECTING IMPERILED
WILDLIFE.

01:01:34.257 --> 01:01:37.126
THESE ONGOING EFFORTS CAN AND
SHOULD, AT A MINIMUM,

01:01:37.193 --> 01:01:39.262
CONSIDER 30 BY 30 AND ALIGN WITH

01:01:39.328 --> 01:01:40.596
THEM WHEREVER POSSIBLE.

01:01:41.064 --> 01:01:42.765
SOME EXISTING EFFORTS NATURALLY

01:01:42.832 --> 01:01:44.067
ALIGN WITH 30 BY 30 GOALS

01:01:44.133 --> 01:01:46.769
AND CAN PROVIDE IMPORTANT
CONSERVATION CO-BENEFITS.

01:01:46.836 --> 01:01:48.337
FOR EXAMPLE, AS PART OF THE
STATE

01:01:48.404 --> 01:01:49.372
WATER BOARD'S REGULATORY

01:01:49.439 --> 01:01:51.307
PROCESS TO SET URBAN OUTDOOR

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:52.708
WATER EFFICIENCY TARGETS,

01:01:52.775 --> 01:01:54.811
THE BOARD IS CONSIDERING HOW
TRANSFORMING URBAN

01:01:54.877 --> 01:01:56.913
LANDSCAPES TO BE MORE DROUGHT
TOLERANT

01:01:56.979 --> 01:01:59.615
CAN ALSO HELP SUPPORT
BIODIVERSITY LIKE

01:01:59.682 --> 01:02:01.284
NATIVE PLANTS AND POLLINATORS.

01:02:01.784 --> 01:02:04.020
ON THE OTHER HAND, FAILING TO
CONSIDER NATURE BASED

01:02:04.087 --> 01:02:08.524
SOLUTION RISKS MINIMIZING OR MIS
MISSING MUTUALLY

01:02:08.591 --> 01:02:11.994
BENEFICIAL OPPORTUNITIES OR
SETTING POLICIES THAT

01:02:12.061 --> 01:02:14.530
UNDERMINE OUR PROGRESS TO
ACHIEVE 30 BY 30,

01:02:15.064 --> 01:02:16.866
THE LEGISLATURE AND THE
ADMINISTRATION

01:02:16.933 --> 01:02:19.102
HAVE MADE GREAT STRIDES SETTING
POLICY

01:02:19.168 --> 01:02:21.871
AND PROVIDING FUNDING IN RECENT
YEARS TO BUILD

01:02:21.938 --> 01:02:24.173
MOMENTUM FOR 30 BY 30 IN
CALIFORNIA.

01:02:24.240 --> 01:02:26.709
